<title>CANADA: Falconbridge appoints Hushovd CEO.</title>
<headline>Falconbridge appoints Hushovd CEO.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Falconbridge Ltd said on Monday that its board of directors had appointed Oyvind Hushovd to replace the recently deceased Frank Pickard as the company's president and chief executive officer.</p>
<p>Hushovd, currently executive vice-president of Falconbridge, has been with the company for 22 years.</p>
<p>&quot;In Oyvind Hushovd, we have a candidate who combines all of the skills necessary to do the job, with an extensive knowledge of Falconbridge, its operations and its people,&quot; said Falconbridge Chairman Alex Balogh.</p>
<p>The decision caps a 10-week search to find a replacement for Pickard who died suddenly during a business trip to Chile in late September.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
